# Shell scripts must stay LF in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the Git for Windows
# default) writes CRLF, and `bash scripts/verify-linux.sh` under WSL dies at
# `set -euo pipefail` with "set: pipefail: invalid option name" — the one
# local check that catches Linux-only failures was silently unrunnable.
*.sh text eol=lf
